{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.node.tsbuildinfo",
    "target": "es2023",
    "lib": ["ES2023"],
    "types": ["node"],
    "skipLibCheck": true,

    /* Bundler mode */
    "module": "nodenext",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": true,
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "noEmit": true,

    /* Linting */
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "erasableSyntaxOnly": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true
  },
  "include": ["vite.config.ts", "middleware.ts", "lib/**/*.ts", "api/**/*.ts"],
  /* api/devnet, api/mainnet, api/kpis, and api/ledger each have their own commonjs/
     node-resolution tsconfig + CommonJS-scoping package.json.
     lib/reserve-activity, lib/reserve-metadata, lib/reserve-image, and
     lib/ledger each have their own CommonJS-scoping package.json (like
     src/merge/lib's) so ts-mocha can require() their pure logic directly
     in tests -- which conflicts with this project's nodenext module
     detection if checked here directly. All are still fully typechecked
     transitively via each isolated api directory's own tsconfig.json
     imports.

     api/kpis and api/ledger are each DEDICATED, fully isolated directories
     (2026-08-18), deliberately separate from api/dashboard (which stays
     governed by this project, unchanged -- its login.ts/content.ts/
     logout.ts have no lib/reserve-activity or lib/ledger dependency and
     never needed a CommonJS override) and from EACH OTHER. Giving the KPI
     dashboard's DB-touching endpoints their own tsconfig.json+package.json
     INSIDE api/dashboard itself was tried first and caused a real
     production incident: Vercel's per-function builder picked up that new
     config for the WHOLE directory, silently changing how it compiled the
     pre-existing login.ts/content.ts/logout.ts and breaking
     /internal/status's login entirely (docs/project/DECISION_LOG.md's
     DEC-0109). A second incident in the same pass (DEC-0109's later entry)
     traced a raw, try/catch-invisible crash to api/kpis/kpis.ts
     synchronously require()-ing lib/road-to-mainnet/auth.ts, a genuine ESM
     module (ERR_REQUIRE_ESM) -- api/kpis/_session.ts and api/ledger/
     _session.ts are each a small, deliberately duplicated, fully
     CommonJS-native auth helper for exactly this reason: nothing under
     api/kpis/ or api/ledger/ may EVER import from lib/dashboard/ or
     lib/road-to-mainnet/, or from each other, or from api/dashboard/. */
  "exclude": ["api/devnet", "api/mainnet", "api/kpis", "api/ledger", "lib/reserve-activity", "lib/reserve-metadata", "lib/reserve-image", "lib/reserve-entry-price", "lib/ledger", "lib/rate-limit"]
}
